Third-party work this project builds on
----------------------------------------

Gadgetbridge (https://gadgetbridge.org, https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge)
  Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0.
  The Garmin support in this app (packages com.animesh.fitnesstracker.garmin.ble,
  .gfdi, .sync, .fit and .workout) was written in Kotlin for this project, but its
  understanding of Garmin's Bluetooth protocol (Multi-Link handles, the reliable
  channel, COBS framing, GFDI message ids and layouts, the file download and upload
  sequences, the capability bitmap) and of the undocumented FIT messages the watch
  writes (stress and Body Battery, sleep stages and scores, HRV status, training
  metrics) comes from studying Gadgetbridge's implementation and its FIT profile.
  That is why this project is released under the same license.

Garmin FIT protocol (https://developer.garmin.com/fit/)
  The FIT file format and the documented message profile are Garmin's public
  specification. No Garmin SDK code is included. Garmin, Forerunner and Body
